{"id":163723895,"slug":"ketamine-in-the-land-of-taylor-swift","title":"Ketamine in the Land of Taylor Swift","subtitle":"An interview with Dr. Irfan Handoo","post_date":"2025-06-20T11:40:28.097Z","audience":"everyone","type":"podcast","canonical_url":"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/ketamine-in-the-land-of-taylor-swift","wordcount":181,"source":"api","fetched_at":"2026-09-13T21:47:07.094Z","body_sha256":"eaea2267a3c7f4c38b634140c9f90124b5cdcc9eecc7b90a1183df8c235fb27d","text_words":182,"complete":true,"body_html":"<p>One of my great joys as a psychiatrist is the ability to collaborate with excellent colleagues.  Irfan Handoo, M.D., of <a href=\"https://kcpsychiatrypartners.com\">Kansas City Psychiatric Partners</a>, is one such human.  </p><p>In this interview, we learn about how Dr. Handoo went from psychopharmacologist to interventional psychiatrist, why Kansas City is the best city in the world, and why being South Asian is the ultimate hack to get your patients the best care.  It's really easy to think of doctors being completely burned out, and not caring about their patients.  Being a physician is a tremendously challenging thing to do with one’s time, and many doctors have their compassion wear thin.  This interview with Dr Handoo reminded me how much some of us care, all day, every day.  He's an inspiration to me, and I hope, to my listeners also.</p><p>I am delighted to bring you this interview! </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!viWr!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe092fcb8-27fc-413d-b265-4e5d054af0f1_1270x672.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!viWr!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%